      "order": "M3",
      "label": "Hydraulic manifold base plate milling",
      "machine_hours": 1,
      "revenue": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x4",
      "order": "M4",
      "label": "Turbine blade precision grinding lot",
      "machine_hours": 3,
      "revenue": 9
    },
    {
      "variable": "x5",
      "order": "M5",
      "label": "Injection mold polymer insert run",
      "machine_hours": 1,
      "revenue": 3
    },
    {
      "variable": "x6",
      "order": "M6",
      "label": "Medical device housing CNC run",
      "machine_hours": 2,
      "revenue": 7
    },
    {
      "variable": "x7",
      "order": "M7",
      "label": "Defence optics mount lathing batch",
      "machine_hours": 2,
      "revenue": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x8",
      "order": "M8",
      "label": "Marine propeller blade casting",
      "machine_hours": 1,
      "revenue": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x9",
      "order": "M9",
      "label": "Industrial gear housing boring batch",
      "machine_hours": 2,
      "revenue": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x10",
      "order": "M10",
      "label": "Electronic enclosure sheet-metal press",
      "machine_hours": 1,
      "revenue": 4
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "type": "budget_inequality",
      "expression": "x1 + 2x2 + x3 + 3x4 + x5 + 2x6 + 2x7 + x8 + 2x9 + x10 <= 12",
      "description": "The machining floor has a total of 12 machine-hours available for this week's production run. The sum of machine-hours for all selected orders must not exceed this budget."
    },
    {
      "type": "tooling_conflict",
      "expression": "x2 * x6 = 0",
      "description": "M2 (aerospace titanium bracket) and M6 (medical device housing) both require the plant's sole 5-axis CNC milling head configuration. At most one can be scheduled this week."
    },
    {
      "type": "tooling_conflict",
      "expression": "x4 * x7 = 0",
      "description": "M4 (turbine blade grinding) and M7 (defence optics mount lathing) both require the same precision metrology fixture for in-process verification. At most one can be scheduled."
    },
    {
      "type": "material_conflict",
      "expression": "x1 * x4 = 0",
      "description": "M1 (brake caliper casting) and M4 (turbine blade grinding) both require the same titanium alloy stock from the materials store, which has only one order's worth of inventory this period."
    }
  ],
  "num_variables": 10
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_manufacturing_production_plan():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: feasible_objective_quality, constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, evaluation_cost, achieved_revenue, selected_orders, total_machine_hours
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

